rose prose-gray dark:prose-invert" data-page-title=3D"Interrupts" data-page=
-href=3D"/oss/python/langgraph/interrupts" id=3D"content"><span data-as=3D"=
p">Interrupts allow you to pause graph execution at specific points and wai=
t for external input before continuing. This enables human-in-the-loop patt=
erns where you need external input to proceed. When an interrupt is trigger=
ed, LangGraph saves the graph state using its <a class=3D"link" href=3D"htt=
ps://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/persistence">persistence</a> l=
ayer and waits indefinitely until you resume execution.</span>
<span data-as=3D"p">Interrupts work by calling the <code>interrupt()</code>=
 function at any point in your graph nodes. The function accepts any JSON-s=
erializable value which is surfaced to the caller. When you=E2=80=99re read=
y to continue, you resume execution by re-invoking the graph using <code>Co=
mmand</code>, which then becomes the return value of the <code>interrupt()<=
/code> call from inside the node.</span>
<span data-as=3D"p">Unlike static breakpoints (which pause before or after =
specific nodes), interrupts are <strong>dynamic</strong>=E2=80=94they can b=
e placed anywhere in your code and can be conditional based on your applica=
tion logic.</span>
<ul>
<li><strong>Checkpointing keeps your place:</strong> the checkpointer write=
s the exact graph state so you can resume later, even when in an error stat=
e.</li>
<li><strong><code>thread_id</code> is your pointer:</strong> set <code>conf=
